    "title": "Lowest Common Ancestor in a Binary Tree",
    "category": "Trees",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "Given the root of a binary tree and two distinct nodes, determine their lowest common ancestor. The lowest common ancestor is the deepest node that has both given nodes as descendants.",
